# m2asc workflow

Living plan: `docs/implementation.md` (see also `docs/__spec.md`).

## Status icons (plan only)

| Icon | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `⬜` | pending — not started |
| `⏳` | in progress — claimed; coding |
| `🔍` | under review — implementation done; awaiting review |
| `✅` | completed — approved and committed locally |

Keep the Contents TOC and the leaf body status in sync.

## Claiming work

Follow the plan’s **Agent playbook**, **Needs**, **Files**, **Hot files**, and **Locked layout**.

1. Read the plan; note every leaf that is `⏳` or `🔍` and the **Files** it owns.
2. Pick the next `⬜` leaf that (a) has all **Needs** leaves `✅`, and (b) **Files** do not overlap any `⏳`/`🔍` leaf (respect **Hot files** — one agent at a time).
3. Set that leaf to `⏳` in Contents and body **before** editing code.
4. Implement **only** that leaf; put new code on the **Locked layout** paths.

All agents share one folder — status on disk is the lock. Do not commit intermediate status flips (`⬜`→`⏳`→`🔍`); only commit the plan when shipping (`✅`).

## Commands

- `/m2asc-next` — claim + implement next leaf; propose commit message; set `🔍`
- `/m2asc-review` — review this leaf’s pending diff; do not commit or push
- `/m2asc-ship` — after human approval: mark `✅`, stage only this leaf (hunk-filter shared files), verify `git diff --cached`, commit locally; **never push**

**Never commit** unless the user runs `/m2asc-ship` or explicitly asks to commit in that message (see `m2asc-no-commit`). Phrases like “separate commits” or “go ahead” alone are not enough. **Never push** — not even if the user asks (see `m2asc-no-push`).
